[candidate · 7:08] Okay, the picture is quite clear. Labor is flat, 22 percent all three years. Overhead moves 12 to 14, so plus two points — small, maybe inflation on rent. But COGS goes 42, 50, 58. That is plus 16 points, and the total profit decline is 18 points. So COGS explain almost ninety percent of the problem.

